🐧Linux Performance & Deep Debugging Commands Every Cloud & DevOps Engineer Should Know:

When dashboards aren’t enough, you drop to the OS.

These 10 commands are used during real production incidents 👇
 

1. strace -p <PID> -c

Trace system calls of a running process with summary counts. Find what it’s waiting on.

2. perf top -p <PID>

Live CPU profiling of a process.
See hot functions instantly.

3. tcpdump -i eth0 -w capture.pcap port 8080

Capture traffic on port 8080.
Deep network debugging.

4. ab -n 10000 -c 100 http://localhost/

Apache Bench load test.
10k requests, 100 concurrent.

5. kubectl debug node/node1 -it --image=busybox

Attach ephemeral container to debug a node.

6. dmesg -T | grep -i 'oom'

Check kernel OOM kill events with timestamps.

7. lsof -i :8080

See which process is using port 8080.

8. iostat -xz 1 5

Disk I/O stats every second (5 intervals).

9. vmstat -w 1 5

Memory, swap, and CPU stats in real time.

10. kubectl debug pod/app -it --copy-to=debug-pod --image=nicolaka/netshoot
